{%- comment -%}
  "Pairs well with" — complementary products, curated.

  Fetched by app.js from
    /recommendations/products?product_id=<id>&intent=complementary&section_id=complementary-products
  which hands this section a `recommendations` object holding the products the
  merchant has paired with this one.

  ── Why curated and not computed ─────────────────────────────────────────

  The guide asks for "frequently bought together, from order co-occurrence
  data or manual curation". Co-occurrence was measured against this store's
  real orders before building anything, and it is not there:

      216 of 250 orders contain a single product   (86%)
       33 orders contain two or more               (13%)
      136 distinct product pairs in total
        8 pairs occur twice
        1 pair occurs three times or more

  Across 1,308 products, a pair seen twice is noise. Recommending on it would
  be asserting a relationship between two fragrances that nothing supports —
  the same class of invention as the testimonials and the stock counters that
  were removed from this theme, just harder to spot because it looks like a
  recommendation engine.

  So this reads Shopify's complementary products, which a human sets in the
  Search & Discovery app (free, first-party) under a product's Related
  products. Nothing renders until someone does. An empty strip here is the
  correct state, not a broken one: it means no pairing has been asserted yet.

  Worth revisiting once the catalogue has a few hundred multi-item orders.
  The query to re-measure is in scripts/, and the test is simply whether
  pairs start recurring.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if recommendations.performed and recommendations.products_count > 0 -%}
  <section class="related">
    <div class="related-inner">
      <div class="related-head fade-up">
        <span class="label">Wears Well Together</span>
        <h2 class="sec-title">Pairs Well <em>With</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="products-grid">
        {%- for product in recommendations.products limit: 4 -%}
          {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{ "name": "Complementary products", "settings": [] }
{% endschema %}
